# Funk: a sixteenth-note groove at ~100. Drums from the Groove MIDI Dataset (drummer 7, a funk groove at 100
# with ghost notes all over the snare, CC BY 4.0: styles/README.md), the rest written for Polly over C M7.
# Written for dominant and minor sevenths: the B of C M7 is the chord's 7th (Bb over C7 and Cm7), so the
# clavinet's E + B is the 3rd and 7th of any chord, the guitar's E + B + D its 3rd, 7th and 9th.
# Main A: bass with octave pops, clavinet in sixteenths, a guitar chank on 2 and 4. Main B: the open hi-hat
# groove, a busier bass, guitar scratches, brass stabs, tambourine.
style Funk
tempo 100

track d1 type=bypass chan=10 vol=104 rev=24
track d2 type=bypass chan=10 vol=104 rev=24   # shares channel 10 with d1: the same mixer
track pc type=bypass chan=10 vol=104 rev=24
track ba type=bass program=33 chan=2 lo=E1 hi=G3 hikey=F# vol=108 rev=8
track c1 type=chord1 program=7 chan=3 lo=Bb3 hi=Bb5 hikey=F# vol=78 pan=40 rev=20
track c2 type=chord1 program=27 chan=4 lo=G3 hi=D6 hikey=F# vol=64 pan=90 rev=30 cho=30
track c3 type=chord2 program=61 chan=5 lo=G3 hi=E5 vol=78 pan=70 rev=40

[main a]
bars 2
beats 4
track d1
drums from=drums/drummer7-session2-72_funk_100_beat_4-4.mid start=36 bars=2 scale=kick:130,chh:85,ohh:85
track ba
# the one, a ghost, the octave pop; the b7 below; the fifth with the kick; a pickup 3-5 into the next bar
1.1.0  C2 5 112
1.1.12 C2 3 62
1.1.18 C3 4 96
